WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.200
Echo checks a proposed evaluation split against training audio.
Index the references, audit the queries, then review the evidence.

00:08.200 --> 00:10.200
Synthetic example. The renamed crop is two seconds long.

00:10.200 --> 00:14.200
[The four-second reference sweep plays.]

00:15.100 --> 00:17.100
[The two-second copied section plays.]
Echo finds the reference at +0.752 seconds.

00:18.200 --> 00:20.200
[A separately generated sweep plays.]
Echo returns no match.

00:20.200 --> 00:24.000
The crop's known start is +0.750 seconds.
The reported timestamp differs by two milliseconds.

00:24.000 --> 00:35.000
The offline report shows decisions, ranks, votes, and time intervals.
Listen to accepted hits. Investigate short, silent, or uncovered queries.

00:35.000 --> 00:46.000
A published ticking-clock case was declined at an incorrect offset.
An independent waveform check found four shared windows at zero seconds.

00:46.000 --> 00:59.000
On the same 400 ESC-50 test clips, mean accuracy was 47.4% with independent
training crops and 57.0% with excerpts of test recordings, a 9.6-point gain.

00:59.000 --> 01:09.000
333 of 360 matching trials were accepted correctly. Echo found 137 of 140
waveform-confirmed pairs at the supported offset. Rust cut measured median query time by 56%.
